1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,735
Tomi compares historical Encyclopaedia Britannica with modern Wikipedia.

2
00:00:03,735 --> 00:00:09,337
Start in the web workspace, choose a model, and ask a question.

3
00:00:09,337 --> 00:00:18,207
English, Spanish, German and French interfaces, theme controls and an anonymous demo session make the same research workflow accessible.

4
00:00:18,207 --> 00:00:24,332
We sampled one hundred historical scans without replacement using a fixed seed and pinned revision.

5
00:00:24,332 --> 00:00:30,456
Every image has a checked hash and a real Nemotron Parse three point five receipt.

6
00:00:30,456 --> 00:00:34,948
Ninety-five pages contain full extracted text; one astronomy plate remains partial.

7
00:00:34,948 --> 00:00:39,847
Three blank leaves and one non-text cover remain visible, without invented prose.

8
00:00:39,847 --> 00:00:46,843
The archive pairs each original scan with a compiled document, raw parsing output and provenance.

9
00:00:46,843 --> 00:00:52,905
Open an individual PDF, download the combined volume, or inspect the editable LaTeX.

10
00:00:52,905 --> 00:00:57,569
The hundred source documents become one hundred eighty-seven compiled pages.

11
00:00:57,569 --> 00:01:01,300
Successful extraction does not certify every OCR character.

12
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,677
The architecture separates model responsibilities.

13
00:01:03,677 --> 00:01:05,104
Parse reads scans.

14
00:01:05,104 --> 00:01:08,909
Embed represents text, and Rerank scores retrieved candidates.

15
00:01:08,909 --> 00:01:13,189
Those two models run on our assigned Nebius GPU.

16
00:01:13,189 --> 00:01:16,517
LanceDB stores vectors in Azure Blob storage.

17
00:01:16,517 --> 00:01:23,175
Super VL comes through Nebius Token Factory and powers the actual Hermes evidence tool.

18
00:01:23,175 --> 00:01:26,980
Rust services keep provider credentials outside the browser.

19
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:32,667
Here we choose Nemotron Super VL and ask a bounded comparison about shipbuilding.

20
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:37,480
The original question stays separate from the topic used for discovery.

21
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:42,730
The application streams progress, shows tool activity, and keeps unsupported answers visible.

22
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:45,792
A completed request still requires source review.

23
00:01:45,792 --> 00:01:51,478
Open the sources to inspect historical and modern passages, pinned revisions and citations.

24
00:01:51,478 --> 00:01:54,540
The trace shows retrieval and model calls.

25
00:01:54,540 --> 00:02:02,412
Our Hermes extension lets the model select immutable span identifiers; the server binds exact quotes and Unicode offsets.

26
00:02:02,412 --> 00:02:05,474
Unknown spans and altered quotations are rejected.

27
00:02:05,474 --> 00:02:10,483
The evidence canvas and three-dimensional graph organize the conversation’s actual sources.

28
00:02:10,483 --> 00:02:13,214
Reload restores the saved conversation evidence.

29
00:02:13,214 --> 00:02:15,946
Export preserves the conversation for review.

30
00:02:15,946 --> 00:02:22,776
Steering and cancellation let you control a running request instead of silently replacing the question.

31
00:02:22,776 --> 00:02:26,874
Source availability and uncertainty stay connected to the answer.

32
00:02:26,874 --> 00:02:32,649
The reviewed shipbuilding case contrasts timber shelf-pieces with the definition of a shipyard.

33
00:02:32,649 --> 00:02:37,090
Both measurement excerpts associate a litre with a cubic decimetre.

34
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:41,977
Bleaching compares vessels and gas with the purpose of removing colour.

35
00:02:41,977 --> 00:02:46,419
These are deliberately narrow coverage observations, reviewed against their citations.

36
00:02:46,419 --> 00:02:48,640
Independent human certification remains pending.

37
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,950
The earlier broad questions failed.

38
00:02:50,950 --> 00:03:01,580
Shipbuilding retrieval favored companies, measurement retrieval returned policy instead of unit definitions, and noisy bleaching OCR could not support a full process comparison.

39
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:04,815
We retain those original outputs and abstentions.

40
00:03:04,815 --> 00:03:09,899
Narrow successes do not erase these failures or establish general accuracy.

41
00:03:09,899 --> 00:03:12,990
All hundred pages are accounted for.

42
00:03:12,990 --> 00:03:21,233
Ninety-six textual or partial pages completed semantic retrieval and reranking: twenty-three candidates and seventy-three ambiguous outcomes.

43
00:03:21,233 --> 00:03:23,808
Four non-text pages stay unmatched.

44
00:03:23,808 --> 00:03:29,990
The analysis records vocabulary overlap and normalized frequencies with both source revisions.

45
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:35,142
Scores are not truth probabilities, and OCR noise limits interpretation.

46
00:03:35,142 --> 00:03:38,295
The platform also generates images from a prompt.

47
00:03:38,295 --> 00:03:41,841
This ship illustration was created through the deployed application.

48
00:03:41,841 --> 00:03:46,570
It is labelled as generated content and does not become historical evidence.

49
00:03:46,570 --> 00:03:50,905
The model selector makes the provider used for each capability visible.

50
00:03:50,905 --> 00:03:55,613
Open speaker separation and select the official thirty-second audio sample.

51
00:03:55,613 --> 00:04:01,261
The deployed Nemotron diarization model returns six segments across five anonymous labels.

52
00:04:01,261 --> 00:04:06,439
Recording and upload are bounded to sixty seconds and one megabyte.

53
00:04:06,439 --> 00:04:10,205
This is batch speaker segmentation, without identity recognition.

54
00:04:10,205 --> 00:04:14,912
Realtime session issuance was tested; physical microphone playback was not.

55
00:04:14,912 --> 00:04:19,964
The pitch deck includes actual solution captures and editable Mermaid diagrams.

56
00:04:19,964 --> 00:04:26,393
Six application services are deployed, with the web service as the public entry point.

57
00:04:26,393 --> 00:04:32,823
The repository includes setup, sample selection, compiled documents, comparison analysis and all six cases.

58
00:04:32,823 --> 00:04:39,712
This walkthrough stays under five minutes; the separate submission cut follows the brief’s three-minute limit.
